OK, then what about using the turn-average system throughout the whole
game?

This means that for every two player turns, game time moves forward
one turn. This way, if either both players move once, then the
monsters and lamps and everything advance one unit in time as well...
or if one player idles and the other player moves twice, the same one
unit of time passes. It would basically average the player moves and
calculate the game turns from that.

I think this could work.

